WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.000
Read the brain. Learn the individual response. Adapt stimulation to the neural state.

00:00:05.000 --> 00:00:13.000
Extract candidate disease-related features; estimate a continuous neural state and its uncertainty.

00:00:13.000 --> 00:00:23.000
Calibrator: learn how this individual responds before adaptive control begins.

00:00:23.000 --> 00:00:30.000
The controller proposes bounded updates; the safety supervisor decides whether output may occur.

00:00:30.000 --> 00:00:38.000
tTIS example: two carrier channels create a difference-frequency envelope. Verify actual delivery.

00:00:38.000 --> 00:00:47.000
Measure again and adapt from trusted feedback. Wait through artifact or uncertain windows.

00:00:47.000 --> 00:00:54.000
Adapt within sessions; use verified records to suggest personalized parameters for the next session.
